~ Introduction
The Arbiter: You have done well to make it this far.
The Arbiter: Tell me, with everything you’ve seen, have you truly grasped your freedom?
The Arbiter: I suppose we shall see…

 => END

~ Doom
The Arbiter: The weight of your actions has kept you shackled to the earth.
The Arbiter: If you truly desire freedom, then you must reflect on what you’ve done, and grow from it.

 => END

~ Perfect
The Arbiter: You have done well. 
The Arbiter: You have aided your fellows in their struggles, and come out of your prison with a spirit that is bright and clear.
The Arbiter: Speak to them, if you wish. Then, when you are ready, you are free to leave.

 => END

~ Good
The Arbiter: You are well along the path to freedom. Your work has born fruit, and you are the lighter for it.
The Arbiter: Speak with your fellows, and reflect on your journey. I am sure the answer will come to you in time.

 => END


~ Neutral
The Arbiter: You traveled far to get to this place, but did your eyes see everything along the path?
The Arbiter: Your fellows struggled and yearned for freedom themselves.
The Arbiter: Reach out to them, perhaps they hold the answers you seek.
The Arbiter: For now, you may rest, and reflect on all that you have seen.

 => END